Patch for helm.sh/helm/v4, applied only to ocm CLI builds (task build:helm in
Taskfile.yml) through a go.work replace. Plain `go build`/`go test` use upstream helm.

helm links k8s.io/client-go/kubernetes and .../kubernetes/scheme, whose init()
registers every k8s.io/api type, via three imports the CLI never exercises.
Cutting all three removes ~16 MB (~35%) from the binary; any one left in place
keeps everything linked.

1. internal/version: blank import of client-go/kubernetes, only there so
   build info lists client-go (still true via pkg/helmpath).
2. pkg/chart/common: default .Capabilities.APIVersions read from the client-go
   scheme; replaced with a snapshot for the k8s.io/client-go version selected
   by bindings/go/go.mod (v0.37.0). Refresh it when client-go is bumped.
3. pkg/getter: All() and plugin getters import pkg/cli -> k8s.io/cli-runtime.
   OCM builds its own providers (helm/internal/download.GetterProviders).

If this stops applying after a helm bump, regenerate it against the new version.

